  ["Hypothermia", "With unwarmed blood", "Cold blood cools the core and impairs clotting.", "In-line warming."],
  ["TA-GVHD", "1 to 6 weeks later", "Donor white cells attack the recipient: fever, rash, diarrhea and bone marrow failure; usually fatal.", "Prevented by irradiation; a known risk of fresh whole blood, especially from related donors."],
  ["Delayed hemolytic reaction", "3 to 14 days later", "Falling hemoglobin, jaundice and fever from antibodies to minor antigens.", "Usually supportive; documented for future transfusions."],
  ["Transfusion-transmitted infection", "Weeks to months", "HIV, hepatitis and other infections; very rare with screened products, higher with emergency fresh whole blood.", "Lookback testing of recipients."]
