      ["Oxygen and pressure support", "Continuous positive airway pressure or lung-protective ventilation as the edema develops."],
      ["Methylene blue if methemoglobinemia is significant", "For cyanosis with a saturation gap that oxygen does not correct, under medical direction."],
      ["Corticosteroids", "Used for the delayed bronchiolitis obliterans phase, where the evidence is better than for the acute phase."],
      ["Documented follow-up", "The casualty is told, in writing, to return for breathlessness or cough in the weeks after discharge."],
      ["Bronchodilators", "For the bronchospasm component."]
